<h2>Topic 1: Introduction to Time Series - Returns, Plots, Stationarity</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Define time series, calculate returns, explain stationarity, read plots.</p>
<p>A time series is data in time order: share price each day, exchange rate each week, claims each month.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Returns:</b> Simple: r = (P_t - P_{t-1}) / P_{t-1}. Log: r = ln(P_t / P_{t-1}). Example: Price 100 to 105. Simple return = 5%. Log return = ln(1.05) = 0.0488 = 4.88%.</p><p><b>Stationary:</b> Mean, variance and correlation do not change over time. Share PRICES are usually not stationary (they wander). RETURNS usually are stationary.</p><p><b>Plot first:</b> Trend? Season? Outliers? Volatility clusters (big jumps follow big jumps)?</p><p><b>White noise:</b> No pattern, mean 0, constant variance, no correlation. If residuals are white noise, your model is good.</p></div>
