<h2>Topic 2: AR, MA and ARMA Models</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~40 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain AR, MA, ARMA, identify order from ACF / PACF, calculate mean and variance.</p>
<p>AR = today depends on yesterday. MA = today depends on yesterday shock. ARMA = both.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>AR(1):</b> Y_t = c + phi Y_{t-1} + e_t. If |phi| &lt; 1, stationary. Mean = c / (1 - phi). Var = sigma^2 / (1 - phi^2).</p><p><b>MA(1):</b> Y_t = mu + e_t + theta e_{t-1}. Always stationary. ACF cuts off after lag 1.</p><p><b>ARMA(1,1):</b> Y_t = c + phi Y_{t-1} + e_t + theta e_{t-1}.</p><p><b>Identify:</b> AR(p): PACF cuts off at p, ACF tails off. MA(q): ACF cuts off at q, PACF tails off.</p><p><b>Example:</b> AR(1), c=2, phi=0.5. Mean = 2 / (1-0.5) = 4.</p></div>
