<h2>Topic 3: ARIMA, Seasonal Models and Forecasting</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~40 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain differencing, ARIMA, seasonal models, make forecasts.</p>
<p>Many series are not stationary. Difference them: Y_t - Y_{t-1}. If still not stationary, difference again. d = number of differences.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>ARIMA(p,d,q):</b> ARMA after differencing d times. Example: ARIMA(1,1,0) = AR(1) on first differences.</p><p><b>Seasonal:</b> Pattern repeats every s periods. Monthly data: s=12. Seasonal differencing: Y_t - Y_{t-12}. SARIMA adds seasonal AR and MA.</p><p><b>Forecast AR(1):</b> 1-step: c + phi Y_t. 2-step: c + phi x (1-step forecast). Forecasts move to mean.</p><p><b>Example:</b> AR(1), c=1, phi=0.6, Y_t=10. 1-step forecast = 1 + 0.6x10 = 7.</p></div>
