<h2>Topic 5: Cointegration, VAR and Financial Time Series in Practice</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain cointegration, VAR, explain how to build a model step by step.</p>
<p>Two series can wander alone but move together long-run. That is cointegration. Example: NSE index and Safaricom price - both wander, but do not drift apart forever.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Cointegration:</b> Two non-stationary series, but a combination of them is stationary. Test: Engle-Granger - regress one on other, test residuals for stationarity.</p><p><b>VAR:</b> Vector Autoregression - two or more series, each depends on past of all. Example: Exchange rate and inflation affect each other, so model them together.</p><p><b>Box-Jenkins steps:</b> 1. Identify (plot, ACF, PACF). 2. Estimate (fit model). 3. Diagnose (residuals white noise?). 4. Forecast.</p></div>
