<div class="topic" id="topic6">
<h2>Topic 6: Time Series in Actuarial Work - Risk, Forecasting, Kenya</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Apply time series to actuarial work, explain VaR, explain Kenya data problems.</p>
<p>Actuaries do not just fit models - they use them to price risk and hold capital.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Uses:</b> 1. Forecast claims, premiums, interest rates. 2. Measure risk - Value at Risk (VaR): worst loss at 95% or 99% confidence. 3. Stress test - what if market falls 20%? 4. Set capital - hold enough to survive bad times.</p><p><b>VaR example:</b> Daily return SD = 2%, mean 0. 95% VaR = 1.65 x 2% = 3.3%. On 100000000 portfolio, VaR = 3300000. Means: 95% chance loss is less than 3300000 in one day.</p><p><b>Kenya:</b> Short series, missing data, thin trading on NSE, shocks (drought, elections) - models must be checked, not trusted blindly.</p></div>
